<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suruga Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suruga Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the central part of present-day Shizuoka Prefecture, on the Pacific coast below <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-fuji">Mount Fuji</a>. Governed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imagawa-clan">Imagawa clan</a> from the 14th century, it was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a> in 1568 and later held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>. Its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunpu">Sunpu</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokaido">Tōkaidō</a> road, is now the city of Shizuoka.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suruga-province.jpg" alt="Suruga Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Suruga.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
